# =============================================================================
# PERILUNE tuning files (.def) — designer-editable sim constants
# =============================================================================
# Every *.def file in this directory is overlaid onto the compiled defaults at
# boot, in filename order (StringComparer.Ordinal). Hosts that load them:
#   - Unity:          Game.View/Bootstrap.LoadDefs
#   - headless tools: tools/ScenarioRunner (and later PeriluneTui) --data
# Sim.Core itself never touches the filesystem: the host reads the text and
# hands (name, text) pairs to Moonbase.Sim.DefsParser.Parse.
#
# This file is comment-only, so it parses with ZERO problems and changes nothing
# — it documents the format and seeds the directory. Delete it freely.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GRAMMAR (see Sim.Core/Defs/DefsParser.cs for the authority)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   # comment          '#' starts a comment to end of line; blank lines ignored.
#   [section]          opens a section; unknown sections are warned + skipped.
#   key = value        scalar sections take one assignment per line.
#   NAME col col ...    the [machines]/[recipes] tables are whitespace-aligned
#                      rows keyed by enum NAME (DeviceKind / ItemKind).
#
# All numbers parse with InvariantCulture ('0.5' is one-half on every machine,
# including de-DE). Booleans accept true/false or 1/0.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECTIONS (field names, units and current values live in Sim.Core/Defs/SimDefs.cs
#           — each field's doc comment records owning system, unit and default)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   [thermal]       lumped-node heat model (ThermalSystem)
#   [atmosphere]    gas flow / consumption / vents / scrubbers (AtmosphereSystem)
#   [needs]         survival thresholds + accumulation rates (NeedsSystem)
#   [sustenance]    eat/drink values (SustenanceSystem)
#   [water]         tank capacity, reclaimer rate + efficiency (WaterSystem)
#   [hydro]         hydroponics irrigation + grow rate (HydroponicsSystem)
#   [wear]          machine wear + maintenance (MachineWear/MaintenanceSystem)
#   [citizen]       movement cadence (CitizenSystem)
#   [exploration]   fog-reveal radius (ExplorationSystem)
#   [machines]      radiator_reject_kw scalar + one row per DeviceKind:
#                     NAME draw gen tier blocks heat wear maint fail
#   [recipes]       one row per crafting DeviceKind:
#                     NAME input in_count output out_count work_s
#
# Example (scalar):    [thermal]
#                      citizen_heat_w = 110
# Example (machine):   [machines]
#                      SolarWing 0 6 Comfort false 0 0.004 0.4 0.1
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTRACT (fail-soft, DeviceLayout precedent)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   - Missing directory / no .def files  ⇒  compiled defaults, silently.
#   - A malformed line                    ⇒  a warning is logged and that single
#                                            value keeps its default. Boot never
#                                            bricks on a bad tuning file.
#   - Only the VALUES that appear here override defaults; everything else stays
#     at SimDefs.CreateDefault().
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HANDOVER INVARIANT (for anyone adding a new tunable)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   A new def field ships in ONE commit with all four of:
#     1. a default in SimDefs.CreateDefault() (today's compiled value, verbatim),
#     2. a parser key/column in DefsParser,
#     3. a fold in SimDefs.ComputeChecksum() (appended at the END so old
#        checksums stay comparable),
#     4. a default-equivalence test (parsed shipped files vs CreateDefault →
#        identical StateHash after N ticks) when a system starts reading it.
#
# The DEFS save chapter stores only SimDefs.Checksum: on load, a checksum that
# differs from the active defs logs a warning and loads anyway (the values come
# from these files, not from the save).
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DESIGNER RULES  (rules/*.moss)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ship-wide automation rules written in MOSS live in the rules/ subdirectory,
# one *.moss file per rule (rule name = filename). They are CONTENT, loaded
# with these defs and folded into the defs checksum — never player state
# (player terminal scripts live in the save; rules do not). Rules run in their
# own interpreter with their own step budget, just before player scripts, so
# a player script wins any same-tick conflict on a device. Rules can read the
# read-only ship.* namespace (power, o2, co2, water, food, heat, morale — all
# normalized 0..1 dashboard values except co2 in ppm; note ship.o2 is a 0..1
# fraction of nominal, NOT a percentage like room o2). alarm() lines land in
# the day-stamped event log. A rule that fails to compile is skipped with a
# diagnostic; the others keep running. Delete a rule file to retire the rule.
